# ZOOMING IN NORMAL PLAY (owner, 2026-09-19: "it shouldnt have to be dev mode,
# just in normal play a user can press + or - to zoom in and out").
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/zoom.tour --seed=4 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0
#
# THERE IS NO --dev ON THAT LINE AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT. The flyover proves
# the same keys work for the owner; this proves they work for a player who can
# never open dev mode. If somebody puts `--dev=` in this header to make it pass,
# the tour has stopped testing anything.
#
# The frames have to show the SAME PLACE at three distances, so that what is
# being proved is the camera moving and not the world changing under it.

wait 0.6
shot 01-where-the-camera-opens with land:coast

# Out. Held, not tapped: a press is a nudge and a hold is a sweep, and the
# ceiling is far enough away that a tap could not reach it.
press zoom_out 1.6
await zoomed_out 3
wait 0.4
shot 02-pulled-back with land:coast

# And in, past where it started, to the near end.
press zoom_in 3.2
await zoomed_in 3
wait 0.4
shot 03-close-in with land:coast

# Back to where a player would leave it, so the last frame of this tour is the
# game as it is normally played.
press zoom_out 1.6
wait 0.6
shot 04-back-to-the-walk with land:coast
